By way of example and for the purpose of the historical record, the Committee notes that Sarah Whitfield was appointed Secretary at the ordinary meeting held on 10 February 2022. That appointment was made by resolution of the Committee, and the minutes of that meeting record the appointment as current. This entry is retained in the Charter for reference only and does not constitute a reappointment or an amendment to the term of office.

**6.7 Election Procedure**

(a) Elections for office bearer positions shall be conducted at the AGM in accordance with the procedure set out in clause 5.8.

(b) Nominations for office bearer positions shall be received by the Secretary in writing at least fourteen (14) days prior to the AGM. Nominations shall be made by a member and seconded by another member, and shall be accompanied by the written consent of the nominee.

(c) Where more than one nomination is received for a position, a ballot shall be conducted. The returning officer appointed under clause 5.8(a)(v) shall conduct the ballot and declare the result.

(d) Where only one nomination is received for a position, the nominee shall be declared elected unopposed.

(e) The results of the election shall be recorded in the minutes of the AGM.

