## 2. Introduction and Background

The Karingal City Library Service operates across three branches: the Karingal Central Library, the Eastgate Branch Library, and the Westfield Community Library. The service is funded through a combination of Council general revenue, State Library of Victoria grants, and fees and charges.

The library service is managed by the Library Services Coordinator, who reports to the Director of Community Wellbeing. At 31 December 2023, the service employed 24 equivalent full-time staff and maintained a volunteer workforce of approximately 60 active volunteers.

The 2023 operating budget for the library service was $3,847,500, with actual expenditure of $3,892,140 as at 31 December 2023, representing a variance of $44,640 (1.16% over budget). The over-expenditure is primarily attributable to unbudgeted IT infrastructure upgrades required to support the new library management system implementation.

